    <briefdescription>
<para>RAII soft chip-select (assert on construct, deassert on destroy). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Use around a single SPI frame (or an intentional multi-byte burst that must stay under one CS assertion). Pair with a bus mutex held for the whole mode + FIFO + transfer window — this guard only owns the CS pin edges.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>Does not replace bus locking. Callers must already own the SPI bus mutex so peers cannot change CPOL/CPHA or steal the peripheral. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
